🔥 Prioritized & Strong Playwright Advantages over Selenium + TestNG

1️⃣ Faster and More Stable Execution

Playwright communicates directly with browsers and uses built-in auto waits, delivering faster execution and eliminating flaky timing issues common in Selenium.

⸻

2️⃣ Lower Maintenance through Auto Waits & Smart Locators

Playwright’s automatic waiting and role-based locators reduce failures caused by UI or timing changes, significantly lowering long-term maintenance effort.

⸻

3️⃣ Rapid Test Creation using CodeGen + GitHub Copilot

Playwright CodeGen records real user actions and generates working scripts instantly, and GitHub Copilot helps refactor this code into clean, reusable methods and page objects, accelerating scalable test development.

⸻

4️⃣ Faster Debugging with Inspector, Debugger & Trace Viewer

Playwright provides Inspector, step-by-step debugging, and Trace Viewer with screenshots, DOM, network, and video—making root-cause analysis much faster than Selenium logs.

⸻

5️⃣ AI-Assisted Migration using GitHub Copilot

Playwright’s modern APIs allow GitHub Copilot to assist in converting Selenium TestNG scripts, reducing migration effort, risk, and manual rewrite.

⸻

6️⃣ Built-In Reporting for Clear Visibility

Playwright offers rich HTML reports with retries, screenshots, and videos out of the box, eliminating the need for external reporting tools.

⸻

7️⃣ All-in-One Framework with Minimal Setup

Playwright includes runner, parallel execution, retries, debugging, and reporting by default, avoiding the heavy configuration and dependency sprawl of Selenium TestNG.